From: UTDeck
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: keep a window of UTDeck's app landscape

The Proton base's version of tools/wine-build/patches/0020 (its patch 0003 differs at this spot).

Lomiri first configures a new window of UTDeck's app as fullscreen portrait (1080x2400 on stone)
and only then applies the app's orientation (landscape-only, from its desktop file) with a
landscape size. Patch 0003 takes the portrait size for a rotated screen, and a resizable window
(wiliwili, a GLFW program, stage 4.5) followed it; Wine then reported an ordinary 1080x2400 window
and Lomiri sent nothing more, so the program stayed portrait in the left part of the landscape
screen. A fixed-size game window (Celceta) never followed and got the landscape size.

A window of UTDeck's app (UTDECK_APP_ID set, patch 0016) with the landscape monitor
(UTDECK_WAYLAND_LANDSCAPE=1, patch 0003) no longer follows a rotation into portrait. Programs
started outside UTDeck keep following the phone.
---
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -652,6 +652,22 @@
          * so the fullscreen window follows it and the application gets a WM_SIZE. */
         BOOL rotated = width && height &&
                        (width > height) != (window_surf_width > window_surf_height);
+        /* Never into portrait for a window of UTDeck's app (UTDECK_APP_ID, patch 0016) with the
+         * landscape monitor (UTDECK_WAYLAND_LANDSCAPE): the app is landscape-only, so a portrait
+         * size is Lomiri's first configure, sent before it applies the app's orientation (the
+         * landscape one follows). A resizable window that followed it stayed portrait for good,
+         * as Lomiri sent nothing more (wiliwili, stage 4.5). */
+        static int landscape_app = -1;
+        if (landscape_app < 0)
+        {
+            const char *app_id = getenv("UTDECK_APP_ID"), *landscape = getenv("UTDECK_WAYLAND_LANDSCAPE");
+            landscape_app = app_id && *app_id && landscape && atoi(landscape);
+        }
+        if (rotated && landscape_app && width < height)
+        {
+            TRACE("hwnd=%p UTDeck's app is landscape: not following %dx%d\n", hwnd, width, height);
+            rotated = FALSE;
+        }
         if (!rotated) flags |= SWP_NOSIZE;
         else TRACE("hwnd=%p fullscreen window follows the rotation to %dx%d\n", hwnd, width, height);
     }
